WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:17.160
Multiple Secondaries have appeared around Fuji!

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.790
Impossible!

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.330
All aircraft near Fuji:
Don't let the enemy near the summit!

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:29.950
Secure an escape route
for those inside at all costs!

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.660
Roger!

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.740
Satomi!

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.200
That's...!

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.080
No... It can't be...

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.990
Mars 2...

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:42.290
Jinguuji's Hero Wing!

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.580
Who?! Who's doing this?!

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.450
The unknown planes identify as downed Valkyrie!

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.830
This can't be!

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.080
Miko!

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:53.830
Guys!

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.700
What the hell is that giant?

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.080
I've never seen anything like--

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.330
Incoming!

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:00.370
Break!

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.330
This maneuvering! It has to be!

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.330
No way...

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.990
All craft, the unknowns are downed Valkyrie.

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:14.290
Please treat them as enemies.
You have permission to fire.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:20.200
Shit! And to think we've loved
and adored these very same Valkyries!

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.580
Who the hell do you guys think you are?!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:59.030
Episode 7:
Fuji Pillar Retreat !

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.330
Shield Squadron under attack!

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:04.080
Enemies number in the forties...
fifties... and increasing!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.990
Our enemies are Valkyries we once fought beside.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:12.740
That much is obvious
by their planes and piloting.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:18.200
After all, we've been saved
by them time and time again.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.540
We remember. How could we forget?

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.410
But, we...

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.290
We didn't remember for this!

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.410
Why isn't the big one moving?

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:40.330
Just ignore it! Focus on the enemies at hand!

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.330
What the?! That thing's wicked fast!

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:54.040
Those marks are Ortlinde! The S-Class Named!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:58.830
Guardian of Japan, Sakura Okita...

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.200
Sakura...

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.200
Japan's Guardian came back as an enemy?!

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.580
I know! Wake me from this nightmare!

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.790
Save the complaints for later! Incoming!

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:22.740
Shit! It's too fast!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.290
It's no use! I'm a goner!

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.160
Not on my watch!

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.200
We'll take over from here!

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.740
Thanks!

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.200
This piloting... It really is Sakura.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.950
Reuniting like this is such a shame.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.790
We're constantly moving forward.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:56.290
The us of today are stronger
than the you of yesterday!

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:59.120
Wow! Just listen to her now!

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.370
I know! Inspiring, right?

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.830
That's our Claudy! You guys are in total sync!

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:08.040
Don't look away! Stay focused, idiot!

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.330
Azu! What should we do?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:14.160
Fighting an old comrade is terrible for morale.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.040
Let's go for the big one.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:19.160
The big one... In that case!

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.160
No way! Nothing?!

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.830
If little guns don't work...

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:32.160
Hero Cannon, fire!

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:35.870
Nice!

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.240
They got past?!

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.160
Kurumi! Don't chase!

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:47.910
Jeez!

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.830
You won't get away!

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:51.790
Yeah!

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:52.910
Look out ahead!

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.120
Huh? Not good!

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:00.080
I went inside?! I've gotta get back!

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:04.120
A black Hero Wing?

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.040
Shoot! I can't shake it!

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.620
Kurumi!

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:09.830
Moe!

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.160
Get out of here!

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.490
Right!

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.370
General...

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.370
Yeah, sorry.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:20.540
Have we located the Vandrande yet?

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.830
There's too much distortion to pinpoint it!

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.700
That sound again...

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:30.580
What's wrong?

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:34.620
Enemies from all over
Japan are swarming this way!

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.620
You're kidding! There's too many!

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.830
R-Radio for--

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:42.740
Abort the operation! Begin a full retreat!

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:49.830
What are you waiting for?
Inform everyone to retreat!

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:54.910
This is command.
All craft, withdraw from battle.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.290
Major General...

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.740
Satomi.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:01.830
Sir?

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:02.870
Onoue.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.410
Sir?

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:05.830
Do me a favor.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:10.240
Abort operation.
All craft, withdraw from battle.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.160
Retreat code 21.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.120
I repeat: abort operation.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.120
Retreat? Why?!

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.120
All craft, withdraw from battle.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:20.700
You heard her! Pillars are
coming from all over Japan!

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.330
Sono! Didn't you hear? Retreat!

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:27.950
I've gotta go help them! Azu, clear us a path!

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:28.620
Wha...?!

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:31.120
I'll do it! Take over for me!

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:32.290
H-Hey!

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:37.080
Azu, they won't listen.
Let's help the others get out of here.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.660
Shit... Just don't forget to retreat.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.700
Shoot! I can't lose 'em!

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:46.080
Leave it to me! Go escape!

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.200
Roger!

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.870
Sorry!

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:57.830
Sonoka! That's enough! Retreat!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.580
But Claudy is still fighting!

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:04.490
She's a Named!
She can see things you guys don't!

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:05.950
Is that why?

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.040
What?

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:10.200
Is that why you went without me?

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.910
Sonoka...

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:15.700
You were a Named. That's why you left me.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.410
Sonoka!

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:22.790
Alice 2?

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:28.290
Sonoka!

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:32.290
Sonoka! Level your plane! Hurry!

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.450
Let's not beat around the bush.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:38.580
What is "Thor" exactly?

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:42.790
I cannot answer that. Not yet.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.410
Someday, in Valhalla...

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.660
Valhalla?

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:50.410
What do you mean by that?

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:56.490
How dare you make us fight our friends!

00:08:56.490 --> 00:09:00.330
Let's put it to rest as fast as we can!

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:02.240
You're done for!

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.240
Liz! Lily!

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:49.450
It stopped!

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.490
Yeah, it stopped.

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:53.870
But...

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.540
This battle...

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:02.490
...has been a complete defeat.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:15.290
Oh, Sono? Are you awake?

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:18.540
Guys! Sono is up!

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.040
Finally awake?

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.620
You had us worried.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.040
C'mon, look this way.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:33.450
Open wide and say "Ah."

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:36.330
Ah...

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.620
No problems for the time being.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:45.080
You're a lucky one. Or maybe unlucky.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:49.040
Still, it's good news that Sonoka's okay.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:52.370
We've had enough bad news for one day.

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:56.620
Miko, Azu, Clo...

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:58.910
What happened after-- Ouch!

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:02.120
Don't push yourself! You're injured!

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:06.660
Did the plan... work out?

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.330
We failed.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:13.620
Do you remember fighting the downed Valkyries?

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:19.200
Yeah... Sakura, the S-Class, was there...

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:26.290
The European girls and I managed
to minimize Ortlinde's damage, but...

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:31.660
That's when the giant moved.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:36.580
It used its weapon to send out
a bolt of lightning and... zap!

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:46.990
It wiped out the majority of our forces.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:49.950
Including command.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:54.700
Command? Don't tell me Satomi was...

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:57.080
Not him too... It's not--

00:11:57.080 --> 00:12:00.580
I'm touched that you're concerned about me.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.830
Satomi!

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:06.870
I made it out just in time.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:11.080
Major General Okita
ordered us to the auxiliary site.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:17.200
While on one hand we're glad
you made it out with the operators...

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:22.830
Major General Okita and
the other officers were wiped out.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:26.660
Odin was there too, and now he's missing.

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:31.120
It's unlikely he survived
that beam of destruction.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:32.490
Mmm.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:39.870
It feels weird to think
that Odie might actually be dead.

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:47.080
But, it's true. That's why we can't afford
to lose any more than we have already.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:53.620
The situation's not good. The giant
and black planes stayed in the Pillar, but...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:59.040
...the Pillars that popped up
in defense still remain a threat.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.790
With this, the operation has officially failed.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:09.990
We must now undertake a large-scale
withdrawal and immediate civilian evacuation.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:12.660
A civilian evacuation?

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:16.870
Remember? The backup
Pillars are wandering around.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:21.580
They're a threat not just to Fuji,
but as far away as Tateyama.

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.450
Tateyama?!

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.870
We're about to deploy again.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:31.580
Leyli... Siegrune was KIA
and Rossweisse is missing.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.540
Right now, every last one of us counts.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.990
Claudy...

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:39.950
Sorry. I'm a little emotional right now.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:41.660
In that case, let me--

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:44.790
What we need is people who can fight.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:51.040
You're injured and your Hero Wing
is in no shape to fly. Hold the fort.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:57.700
You're leaving me behind again?
Even if it means more risk to you guys?

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:02.080
Don't get worked up.
We're just helping with the evacuation.

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:03.490
The ones doing rescue are--

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:05.200
Azu!

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:09.490
What do you mean by "rescue"?

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:14.580
Guys? What are you hiding from me? Tell me!

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:19.660
Watarai, that's--

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:22.910
Satomi, I'll talk to her.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:27.790
Sorry, but could we get some privacy?

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.990
It's been a while since we talked alone.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:37.660
The last time was in the hospital, right?

00:14:37.660 --> 00:14:40.290
Except I was the patient.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.790
What a scary face.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:49.870
You used to call me Big Sister
and cling to my side.

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:51.330
Amatsuka!

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:57.540
Remember that one time I got drunk
and held you like a body pillow all night?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:01.080
After that, we slept together almost every day.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.660
Amatsuka!

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:06.950
You always act like a baby,
plus you're shy around people.

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:10.660
But since you're getting along
with Miko and them, I can rest assu--

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.490
Big Sister!

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:19.160
You finally called me that again.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:24.490
That's one less thing weighing me down.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:28.540
Now I can fly without worry.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.830
We have comrades left behind in the Pillar.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.620
I volunteered for the rescue.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:40.830
We're not about to turn our backs
and abandon our friends.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:47.620
But, it's too dangerous! There's so
many enemies that we had to retreat!

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:54.450
Someone had to step up and do it.
Being a former Named, I'm more than capable.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:58.700
I'm skilled and
experienced--perfect for the job.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:06.580
They came to help with the operation.
I won't abandon any of my cute little sisters.

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:14.950
Oh, come on. Stop your crying.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.660
I won't... I won't...

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:22.540
Unless you don't go, I won't!

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:28.040
I'm sorry for being stubborn!
I'm sorry! I apologize!

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.830
So, don't go...

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:38.700
I have to. I can't protect you if I don't.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:41.160
But, I promise...

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.620
Promise?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:49.580
I promise I'll come back. Remember?
I come back, even when I'm shot down.

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:55.540
I'll hold on to this as a charm.

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:04.450
And for you, I'll lend you this one of mine.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.630
Safe Flight

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:07.160
This... is your...

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:13.200
Keep that close and wait for me.
It doubles the effectiveness of all prayers.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:20.370
And if you're so worried that it gets to be
too much, open it up when the time is right.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:22.990
For some emotional support.

00:17:22.990 --> 00:17:25.990
Big Sister...

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:28.370
Speaking of which...

00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:33.160
You've always been the one
to cheer me up, Sonoka.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:49.790
Shouldn't you be busy with the evacuation?

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:55.870
Our friend is leaving on a heroic mission.
We wanted to see you off.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:57.660
Godspeed!

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:04.790
Good grief, that's so stiff!
Could you loosen it up a bit?

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.080
In that case...

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.370
Good luck!

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:11.990
That's better. Take care--

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:13.700
Big Sis!

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:19.330
Big Sis! What's your favorite food?!
I'll make something for when you come back!

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:24.990
I just can't compete with you.
Meat and potato stew, and don't be skimpy.

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:29.040
Okay, got it. Loaded with meat.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:35.490
This area here should be
outside the Pillars' influence.

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:37.660
We'll wait for you there.

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:40.990
And here I thought you hated me.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:47.870
I do. And everyone else who has a wish to die.
So come back, even if you do.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:53.540
It's a problem if you hate me.
Especially 'cuz I love you so much.

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:14.700
Sherry, huh? You really splurged this time.

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:17.330
It's my secret stash.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:21.410
If you asked me,
I would've preferred high-class saké.

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:27.450
Well, it's plenty fancy enough
for a nice, old-fashioned toast.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:32.790
Usually after the shot, it's tradition
to smash the glass on the ground.

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:38.540
But I made a promise to come back,
so this isn't a farewell drink.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:41.950
This is a toast for good luck! Understand?!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.120
Got it!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:46.660
I'm getting thirsty! Keep your speeches shorter!

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:48.830
It's Big Sis' bad habit!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:53.330
Hmph! Try learning to read
the mood sometimes, guys!

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:54.040
Cheers!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.870
Cheers!

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:01.700
Can I leave Sonoka in your hands?

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:06.990
That's a big responsibility.
Can you not make her cry this time?

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:11.450
That all depends on how this goes.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:15.660
You're rescuing our comrades
from a mountain of enemies.

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:17.540
It's gonna be tough.

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:20.580
I'm used to you asking the impossible.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:22.620
Ain't that the truth.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:25.740
Well, go give 'em hell.

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:28.240
Yeah. Wish me luck.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:42.990
Ready to dive in? What kind of
fools volunteer for this mission?!

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:45.580
If we survive, I'll give you a kiss!

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:47.950
Sorry I'm past my prime!

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.540
Whew! You hear that, guys?!

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.700
If we get a kiss from Big Sis...!

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:55.580
...I'd walk through the fires of hell!

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.870
Hmph! What would your parents say to that?!

00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:01.080
Try to keep up with me!

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:03.370
Aye aye, ma'am!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:06.790
Don't underestimate humans, you monsters!

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:18.130
"Safe Flight"

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:24.700
Hmm?

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:44.040
Can you climb down?

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:46.040
I'll... manage.

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:49.990
You're badly hurt! Hold on, I'll call for help!

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:53.330
How did you know where we were?

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:57.450
She told me. Who here is Sonoka?

00:21:57.450 --> 00:22:00.290
Th-That's me.

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:09.620
This is all... I could bring back.

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:18.040
You... liar...

00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:25.950
You liar! You liar! You liar!

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:33.370
Big Sister! You liar!

00:23:58.160 --> 00:23:59.830
The counteroffensive failed.

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:01.490
Many lives were lost.

00:24:01.490 --> 00:24:03.410
Fuji Pillar still stands.

00:24:03.410 --> 00:24:03.990
But...!

00:24:03.990 --> 00:24:04.620
...hope...!

00:24:04.620 --> 00:24:05.740
...remains!

00:24:05.740 --> 00:24:06.790
Look out, Pillar!

00:24:06.790 --> 00:24:07.490
Don't...!

00:24:07.490 --> 00:24:08.740
...underestimate us!

00:24:08.740 --> 00:24:12.120
I told you we can do a proper preview!

00:24:09.340 --> 00:24:12.120
Episode 8
Exploring a Mythical World !

00:24:09.370 --> 00:24:12.120
Next Time
